  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The Law of Cosines states that\n\n$$\n{c}^{2}={a}^{2}+{b}^{2}-2ab\\operatorname{cos}⁡C.\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nm∠C={43}^{∘},\\,a=10,\\,b=13.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the numbers into the formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}^{2} & ={10}^{2}+{13}^{2}-2(10)(13)\\operatorname{cos}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =100+169-260\\operatorname{cos}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =269-260(0.731\\,35…) \\\\  & =269-190.151\\,96 \\\\  & =78.848\\,04.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places\n\nTaking the square root gives\n\n$$\nc=\\sqrt{78.848\\,04}=8.88\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places.",
